--
--   Description
--
-- This test is intended to cover the transmit functionality of the GEM 
-- in both normal gigabit operation and burst gigabit operation, using the 
-- FIFO interface.
-- 
-- Functional Coverage
----------------------
-- · Ensure there are no errors for transmitted frames with padding insertion 
--   and frame check sum insertion by the GEM (burst and non-burst modes). 
-- · Ensure there are no errors for transmitted frames with no padding 
--   insertion and no frame check sum insertion by the GEM (burst and 
--   non-burst modes).  (Frame check sum is already in frame)
-- 
-- Detailed Test Description
----------------------------
-- Normal Gigabit Operation for Transmitting Frames 
--    with Padding and FCS Inserted:
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for gigabit and transmit operation.
-- 2. Supply a frame that is less than minimum frame size 
--    (with no crc). (This should cause the GEM to insert padding, 
--    FCS and carrier extension)
-- 3. Check status registers and statistic registers and ensure that 
--    the frame was transmitted properly with no errors.
-- 
-- Normal Gigabit Operation for Transmitting Frames 
--    without Padding and FCS Inserted:
-- 4. Supply a frame that is minimum frame size (with crc). 
--    (The GEM should not insert padding, FCS and carrier extension)
-- 5. Check status registers and statistic registers and ensure that the 
--    frame was transmitted properly with no errors.
-- 
-- Burst Gigabit Operation for Transmitting Frames 
--    with Padding and FCS Inserted:
-- 6. In burst mode, supply a frame that is less than minimum frame size 
--    (with no crc).  Then transmit two more frames that are less than 
--    minimum frame size (with no crc). (This should cause the GEM to insert 
--    padding and FCS into all three frames. Also, the first frame of the burst 
--    should have extension added as well.)
-- 7. Check status registers and statistic registers and ensure that the 
--    frame was transmitted properly with no errors.
-- 
-- Burst Gigabit Operation for Transmitting Frames 
--    without Padding and FCS Inserted:
-- 8. In burst mode, supply a frame that is minimum frame size (with crc).  
--    Then transmit two more frames that are less than minimum frame size 
--    (with crc). (The GEM should not insert padding and FCS into all three 
--    frames. Also, the first frame of the burst should have extension added 
--    as well.)
--
-- Burst Gigabit Operation for Transmitting Frames
--    where FCS is inserted/non-inserted within the
--    same burst:
-- 10. Two further frames transmitted as part of the burst, the first with no
--     crc appended, and the second with crc appended.
-- 11. Check status registers and statistic registers and ensure that the 
--     frame was transmitted properly with no errors.
 
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

